{"schema_version": 5, "unit_id": "tag:08MI:statement", "parent_tag": "08MA", "chapter": "defos", "node_kind": "remark", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe a trivial first order thickening of ringed topoi\nand let <MATH_0002> be a trivialization. Then given any triple\n<MATH_0003> consisting of a pair of\n<MATH_0004>-modules and a map\n<MATH_0005>\nwe may set\n<MATH_0006>\nand use the splitting (<REF_0001>)\nassociated to <MATH_0007> and the map <MATH_0008> to define the <MATH_0009>-module\nstructure and obtain an extension (<REF_0002>).\nWe will call <MATH_0010> the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>trivial extension<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of\n<MATH_0011> by <MATH_0012> corresponding\nto <MATH_0013> and the trivialization <MATH_0014>. Given any extension\n<MATH_0015> as in (<REF_0003>) we can use\n<MATH_0016> to think of <MATH_0017>\nas an <MATH_0018>-module extension, hence a class <MATH_0019>\nin <MATH_0020>.\nLemma <REF_0004> assures that\n<MATH_0021>\ninduces a bijection\n<MATHSEG_0001>isomorphism classes of extensions<MATHSEG_0002> as in <MATHSEG_0003> with <MATHSEG_0004>\nMoreover, the trivial extension <MATH_0022> maps to the zero class.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}) \\to (\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}')$", "MATH_0002": "$\\pi : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}') \\to\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\mathcal{F}, \\mathcal{K}, c)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0005": "$c : \\mathcal{I} \\otimes_\\mathcal{O} \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{K}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\mathcal{F}'_{c, triv} = \\mathcal{F} \\oplus \\mathcal{K}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-splitting-ringed-topoi}", "MATH_0007": "$\\pi$", "MATH_0008": "$c$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}'$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{equation-extension-ringed-topoi}", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}'_{c, triv}$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "